{"slug": "barley-corn-and-lobster-salad", "nyt_id": 10654, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10654-barley-corn-and-lobster-salad", "name": "Barley, Corn And Lobster Salad", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 1 ½-pound lobsters", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "1 ½-pound lobsters", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 cups cooked barley, cooled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "cooked barley", "preparation": "cooled", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 ears corn, cooked and kernels cut off cob", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "ears corn", "preparation": "cooked and kernels cut off cob", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 tablespoon fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 teaspoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "3 tablespoons chopped fresh basil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh basil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt, plus more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": "plus more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Steam the lobsters until they turn bright red, about 10 minutes. Set aside until cool enough to handle. Remove the meat and cut into large chunks."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Toss the lobster, barley and corn together. Add the lemon juice, olive oil, basil, salt and pepper. Toss until well combined. Divide among 4 plates and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 427.2, "protein_g": 59.8, "carbohydrates_g": 32.9, "fat_g": 5.9, "saturated_fat_g": 1.2, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 432.0, "sodium_mg": 1449.5, "fiber_g": 4.4, "sugar_g": 3.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["new england"], "diet": ["dairy-free", "low-fat"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner", "lunch"], "occasion": ["fourth of july", "labor day"], "other": ["barley", "corn", "lobster", "salad", "seafood", "steam", "summer"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-07-18", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:30:11.313364+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "bananes-flambees-flamed-bananas", "nyt_id": 785942856, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/785942856-bananes-flambees-flamed-bananas", "name": "Bananes Flambées (Flamed Bananas)", "author": "Pete Wells", "description": "In his classic step-by-step illustrated cookbook “La Technique” (first published in 1976 by Times Books), Jacques Pépin called flamed bananas “an inexpensive and delicious dessert.” And they are. Roasting the bananas in their skins keeps them intact during the initial cooking. Things get trickier once you peel them and introduce them to the caramel sauce. Be gentle. And when it’s time to ignite the rum, watch your fingers. Fireplace matches or one of those butane-fueled grill lighters are helpful, as is a long-handled spoon for basting. Pete Wells", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 5, "cook_minutes": 35, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "40 min", "prep": "PT0H5M", "cook": "PT0H35M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "6 large ripe (not over-ripe) bananas, unpeeled", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large ripe (not over-ripe) bananas", "preparation": "unpeeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ cup/113 grams unsalted butter", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cup/113 grams unsalted butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "⅓ cup/66 grams sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "cup/66 grams sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Juice of 1½ limes", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "juice of 1½ limes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Juice of 1 lemon", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "juice of 1 lemon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¼ cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "⅓ cup good, dark rum", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "good", "preparation": "dark rum", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Vanilla ice cream, for serving (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "vanilla ice cream", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the oven to 400 degrees. Trim off the ends of the bananas. With the point of a paring knife, make an incision down one side of each banana."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place bananas in a roasting pan or on a baking sheet and bake for 15 minutes. The skin will turn black and the bananas will become soft to the touch. Keep at room temperature until serving time."}, {"position": 3, "text": "At serving time, melt the butter in a 10-inch, preferably straight-sided pan (not nonstick) over medium-high heat and stir in the sugar, lime juice, lemon juice and water. Cook for about 5 minutes, until it turns a nice golden caramel color. “Unwrap” the bananas into the sauce."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Using a spoon and fork, flip the bananas over in the sauce. Add the rum and gently shake the pan back and forth briefly to combine. With a long match or a long-handled igniter, carefully ignite."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Using a large, long-handled metal spoon, baste the bananas with the sauce until the flames subside. Remove from the heat."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Serve on warm plates or in shallow bowls, 1 banana per person with sauce, with ice cream alongside if you like."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 324.2, "protein_g": 1.8, "carbohydrates_g": 41.1, "fat_g": 16.0, "saturated_fat_g": 9.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 41.7, "sodium_mg": 6.7, "fiber_g": 3.9, "sugar_g": 26.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 5.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": ["gluten-free", "egg-free", "peanut-free", "tree nut-free", "soy-free", "fish-free", "shellfish-free", "pork-free", "sesame-free", "vegetarian", "pescatarian", "low-sodium"], "course": ["dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["banana", "lime juice", "lemon juice", "rum", "roast", "caramelize", "budget"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/05/multimedia/06FD-PEPIN-BOOKREX-PW-Bananes-Flambees-1-zqml/06FD-PEPIN-BOOKREX-PW-Bananes-Flambees-1-zqml-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "/imagepages/2026/08/03/multimedia/06FD-PEPIN-BOOKREX-PW-Bananes-Flambees-2-hpbz.html", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 8}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-08-05", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:27:20.099694+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "banana-nut-oatmeal", "nyt_id": 787678669, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/787678669-banana-nut-oatmeal", "name": "Banana Nut Oatmeal", "author": "Ali Slagle", "description": "This quick, pantry-friendly oatmeal has banana bread sensibilities: It gets its sweetness from mashed banana and its toastiness from nut butter and cinnamon. Cooking the oats in a combination of milk and water makes it creamy but not stodgy, while a scattering of toasted nuts gives these soft bowls a bit of crunch. (You can add more texture with hemp or flax seeds, too.) If your banana isn’t super ripe, you may want to add some maple syrup for sweetness to balance the earthiness of the nuts and oats.", "servings": {"text": "2 servings", "min": 2, "max": 2, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 10, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "20 min", "prep": "PT0H10M", "cook": "PT0H10M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ½ cups unsweetened non-dairy or whole milk, plus more for serving", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "unsweetened non-dairy or whole milk", "preparation": "plus more for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 cup water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 cup old-fashioned rolled oats", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "old-fashioned rolled oats", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Pinch of salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch of salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 large, ripe banana", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large", "preparation": "ripe banana", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon almond butter", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "almond butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ teaspoon ground cinnamon, plus more for serving", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "ground cinnamon", "preparation": "plus more for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Maple syrup, to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "maple syrup", "preparation": "to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons toasted, chopped nuts, for topping", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "toasted", "preparation": "chopped nuts, for topping", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a large, nonstick skillet, combine the milk, water, oats and a pinch of salt. Bring to a simmer over medium-high, then reduce heat to medium and cook, stirring frequently, until the oats are tender and a spoon dragged through the liquid leaves a trail for a second or two, 5 to 7 minutes. (The oatmeal will thicken off the heat.)"}, {"position": 2, "text": "Remove from the heat. Thinly slice the banana. Add half the banana and all the almond butter and cinnamon to the oatmeal. Smash the banana with a fork, then stir to combine. Taste and if you’d like it sweeter, add maple syrup to taste."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Scoop into bowls and top with the remaining banana slices, nuts and a sprinkle of cinnamon – plus a drizzle of milk and maple syrup if you’d like."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 454.2, "protein_g": 15.3, "carbohydrates_g": 64.0, "fat_g": 17.8, "saturated_fat_g": 4.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 18.3, "sodium_mg": 161.5, "fiber_g": 7.2, "sugar_g": 26.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 10.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["egg-free", "soy-free", "fish-free", "shellfish-free", "pork-free", "sesame-free", "alcohol-free", "vegetarian", "pescatarian", "high fiber", "vegan", "healthy", "dairy-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["breakfast"], "occasion": [], "other": ["non-dairy milk", "milk", "rolled oat", "banana", "almond butter", "ground cinnamon", "nut", "oatmeal", "simmer", "for two", "stovetop", "easy", "quick", "one pot"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/08/26/multimedia/AS-Banana-Nut-Oatmeal-lqkp/AS-Banana-Nut-Oatmeal-lqkp-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 71}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2026-08-26", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:28:28.044325+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
